WEBVTT

00:01:32.400 --> 00:01:34.070
Let's go to Nihonbashi.

00:01:35.740 --> 00:01:40.740
So I guess that means Rikugou-san trusts the tengu and his subordinates, right?

00:01:41.490 --> 00:01:42.490
Huh?

00:01:42.490 --> 00:01:45.200
Ah, um, it doesn't mean as much as that.

00:01:45.200 --> 00:01:46.500
It's just a hunch.

00:01:47.040 --> 00:01:48.330
Right.

00:01:48.330 --> 00:01:50.960
Then let's follow your hunch.

00:01:52.250 --> 00:01:55.510
I'm sorry to interrupt you at an interesting part of the story...

00:01:56.130 --> 00:01:59.010
but what on earth is the Blank Page?

00:02:02.720 --> 00:02:04.770
What?! You don't know?!

00:02:04.770 --> 00:02:07.190
I-Is it bad that I don't know?!

00:02:07.190 --> 00:02:10.520
Come on, now. You guys are talking about difficult things with that all-knowing look!

00:02:10.520 --> 00:02:12.230
Now, explain it!

00:02:12.230 --> 00:02:16.280
I don't know, or perhaps I should say,
I don't believe it that much!

00:02:16.280 --> 00:02:19.780
Isn't that worse than me?!

00:02:20.410 --> 00:02:25.160
Basically, only a few people
know about the Blank Page.

00:02:25.160 --> 00:02:29.830
I'll explain in detail at my house
in Nihonbashi.

00:02:30.210 --> 00:02:32.840
I'm sorry that I'm slow to understand.

00:02:32.840 --> 00:02:38.420
It's more surprising to me that you know about such a highly confidential matter.

00:02:39.220 --> 00:02:43.470
You're a close confidant of Sasaki-dono, not just a minor official.

00:02:44.310 --> 00:02:45.390
Oh, I must've slipped up.

00:02:45.390 --> 00:02:47.100
Don't lie.

00:02:47.100 --> 00:02:48.980
In addition to being in this secular place,

00:02:48.980 --> 00:02:52.610
we are accompanying people who might possibly make matters worse.

00:03:00.410 --> 00:03:01.320
What?

00:03:01.320 --> 00:03:03.070
No, it's nothing.

00:03:03.070 --> 00:03:05.370
Then take your hand off me!

00:03:05.370 --> 00:03:06.870
I can't do that.

00:03:08.540 --> 00:03:09.870
Hey, don't touch me.

00:03:10.540 --> 00:03:12.920
What the hell are you...

00:03:12.920 --> 00:03:17.130
Ouch, ouch, ouch, ouch, ouch,
I got it, I got it.

00:03:17.510 --> 00:03:19.760
Hey, I'll leave you two alone.

00:03:20.050 --> 00:03:23.720
Hey, Kuchiha, if we don't hurry,
we'll get left behind.

00:03:23.720 --> 00:03:25.720
Yeah, I know!

00:03:28.520 --> 00:03:30.480
Young master, welcome back.

00:03:32.100 --> 00:03:34.480
This is my house.

00:03:35.480 --> 00:03:38.780
I'm running a kind of pharmacy.

00:03:39.490 --> 00:03:42.360
Young master, may I talk to you?

00:03:43.030 --> 00:03:44.620
This is really amazing.

00:03:44.620 --> 00:03:46.120
It's quite big and busy.

00:03:46.120 --> 00:03:50.710
That's because Yorozu-ya is
the biggest store around here.

00:03:50.710 --> 00:03:53.210
Young master, who are your companions?

00:03:53.210 --> 00:03:56.500
Oh, they're important friends of Sasaki-sama.

00:03:56.500 --> 00:03:58.590
I'm sorry, but would you take them to the back?

00:03:58.590 --> 00:04:00.760
Okay! Will do.

00:04:00.760 --> 00:04:03.220
Now, everyone. Please come this way.

00:04:11.060 --> 00:04:13.810
Well, in diagram form, it would look like this.

00:04:14.350 --> 00:04:17.320
The three who received part
of Teiten's power are

00:04:17.320 --> 00:04:19.360
Bon, Gyou, and Koku.

00:04:19.360 --> 00:04:23.360
But in some ways, you could say that Rikugou-san here

00:04:23.360 --> 00:04:25.450
has the same power as Teiten.

00:04:25.450 --> 00:04:28.530
Although he doesn't look it at all.

00:04:28.530 --> 00:04:30.790
I think so too. But, Kuchiha,

00:04:30.790 --> 00:04:33.330
it's also said that a talented hawk hides its talon.

00:04:33.330 --> 00:04:35.920
You're no hawk. You're a crested ibis.

00:04:35.920 --> 00:04:36.920
Yeah.

00:04:36.920 --> 00:04:42.010
Bon, Gyou, Koku are all effectively under Teiten's thumb.

00:04:42.010 --> 00:04:44.930
They can only move along
the strands of heaven's net.

00:04:46.180 --> 00:04:53.430
Rikugou-san is the only one who can tear the strands or weave new ones.

00:04:58.110 --> 00:05:00.860
But isn't that what everyone does?

00:05:01.980 --> 00:05:06.160
Most people don't know what
will happen in the future.

00:05:07.410 --> 00:05:11.660
Sure, but the one who knows
the end of the world says

00:05:11.660 --> 00:05:13.910
that keeping matters unchanged
will not be good.

00:05:14.790 --> 00:05:17.880
Gyouten-sama seems to know all about it

00:05:17.880 --> 00:05:20.630
but doesn't say anything
to the common people.

00:05:20.630 --> 00:05:24.220
A beautiful but unexpectedly stingy person.

00:05:24.220 --> 00:05:25.970
You, watch your mouth!

00:05:25.970 --> 00:05:29.180
Oh, sorry. I slipped up again.

00:05:29.850 --> 00:05:31.260
I see.

00:05:31.260 --> 00:05:33.430
Wow, you understood that.

00:05:33.430 --> 00:05:35.730
I grasped it, but I don't agree.

00:05:35.730 --> 00:05:37.900
Yeah, I feel somewhat like that too.

00:05:37.900 --> 00:05:39.940
How irresponsible!

00:05:39.940 --> 00:05:43.610
According to the story,
you seem to be in an extraordinary position.

00:05:43.610 --> 00:05:44.990
Y-Yeah.

00:05:45.610 --> 00:05:49.620
Perhaps the tengu is just
planning to use you?

00:05:49.620 --> 00:05:53.490
Um, didn't I say that they really didn't look that bad to me?

00:05:53.490 --> 00:05:56.370
So you're actually going to trust
the tengu, aren't you?

00:05:56.370 --> 00:06:00.330
Um, didn't I say that rather than trusting him, it's my hunch?

00:06:00.330 --> 00:06:01.090
Huh?

00:06:04.260 --> 00:06:05.510
Are you in a bad mood?

00:06:05.510 --> 00:06:06.220
Yeah.

00:06:06.220 --> 00:06:07.840
You surely must be.

00:06:07.840 --> 00:06:09.640
Isn't that all right?

00:06:10.390 --> 00:06:14.270
The Blank Page is an open canvas, with no biases laid on it.

00:06:15.270 --> 00:06:21.860
It fits your way of not judging others
by whether they're demons or human.

00:06:21.860 --> 00:06:27.190
Putting these complex matters aside,
I can agree with that one point.

00:06:27.780 --> 00:06:29.360
Although it makes me angry too.

00:06:32.870 --> 00:06:34.370
Excuse me.

00:06:35.580 --> 00:06:37.580
I brought some tea.

00:06:37.580 --> 00:06:39.460
Beni-chan, thank you.

00:06:49.680 --> 00:06:51.140
It's a direct hit.

00:06:51.680 --> 00:06:54.430
Lucky that you didn't go on a fool's errand.

00:06:54.430 --> 00:06:55.510
What do you mean?

00:06:57.520 --> 00:07:00.060
Those officers we met a while ago were investigating an incident.

00:07:00.060 --> 00:07:02.610
Two men were behind it:

00:07:02.610 --> 00:07:06.530
a well-known informer, and a doctor suspected of making illegal opium.

00:07:07.030 --> 00:07:09.360
Genkichi, the man who was murdered,

00:07:09.360 --> 00:07:12.490
seems to have been selling opium illegally.

00:07:12.490 --> 00:07:18.200
The officers believe that low-class scum
committed the crime to destroy evidence.

00:07:18.200 --> 00:07:19.540
Opium...

00:07:19.540 --> 00:07:21.080
Drugs.

00:07:21.080 --> 00:07:24.540
So humans committed the murder at Naitou-Shinjuku, right?

00:07:25.460 --> 00:07:28.170
If demons were not involved,
it's none of our business.

00:07:28.170 --> 00:07:33.840
However, there's been quite a lot of talk about seeing will-o'-the-wisps in the neighborhood lately.

00:07:33.840 --> 00:07:36.430
That could be considered strange.

00:07:38.270 --> 00:07:41.980
How about dividing into two groups now?

00:07:42.690 --> 00:07:45.610
I'll go check around there with this young lady.

00:07:45.610 --> 00:07:48.940
In the meantime, the rest of you can wait here.

00:07:50.240 --> 00:07:50.950
Negative.

00:07:51.450 --> 00:07:54.490
I can't leave Shinshu's side.

00:07:54.490 --> 00:07:57.450
How can I leave Shinshu by herself?

00:07:57.830 --> 00:08:01.460
If she wants someone to talk to,
there's my sister.

00:08:01.460 --> 00:08:03.710
She is my dear, proud sister.

00:08:07.840 --> 00:08:09.960
I'm not worried about that!

00:08:09.960 --> 00:08:15.430
If you're concerned about a guard, the person sitting over there seems to be very skilled.

00:08:17.970 --> 00:08:20.060
Apparently she's stronger than you.

00:08:20.060 --> 00:08:21.140
Isn't that reassuring?

00:08:21.140 --> 00:08:24.150
Wh— You think I'm weaker than she is?

00:08:24.150 --> 00:08:27.690
Oh, sorry. I'm naturally honest.

00:08:27.690 --> 00:08:28.570
You...

00:08:33.150 --> 00:08:34.740
Wh-What was that?

00:08:34.740 --> 00:08:35.820
Don't surprise me!

00:08:35.820 --> 00:08:38.030
Oh, sorry, sorry.

00:08:38.990 --> 00:08:41.160
It's just the two of you were
glaring at each other.

00:08:42.200 --> 00:08:44.870
Tsuruume-san, don't take
such a truculent attitude.

00:08:44.870 --> 00:08:47.420
You'll make Shinshu-chan worry in turn.

00:08:48.040 --> 00:08:51.760
Kurotobi-san, you mustn't tease Tsuruume-san,
even if you see she's on edge.

00:08:51.760 --> 00:08:53.470
Oh, how did you know?

00:08:53.470 --> 00:08:55.720
Kurotobi-san, you're probably a bully.

00:08:55.720 --> 00:08:57.180
Oh, how could you know that?

00:09:04.060 --> 00:09:05.520
Never mind, never mind.

00:09:11.780 --> 00:09:13.070
It's unavoidable.

00:09:13.070 --> 00:09:16.070
Since we've made a decision, let's finish quickly and come back immediately.

00:09:16.070 --> 00:09:16.610
Yes.

00:09:16.990 --> 00:09:20.370
On my way, I'll also check whether anything else is happening in town.

00:09:20.370 --> 00:09:21.620
Let's do it carefully.

00:09:22.370 --> 00:09:24.620
Please! I'm counting on you.

00:09:24.620 --> 00:09:26.870
You know what I did?

00:09:26.870 --> 00:09:29.170
They turned me out.

00:09:29.170 --> 00:09:33.710
So I stole all their money
before I ran away from them.

00:09:34.760 --> 00:09:36.680
Don't you think that's going too far?

00:09:36.680 --> 00:09:38.010
They'll probably come after you.

00:09:38.890 --> 00:09:43.970
I'm connected to the notorious
group known as Amaza.

00:09:44.520 --> 00:09:46.480
Even if they don't believe in demons,

00:09:46.480 --> 00:09:49.100
it's common knowledge
that we can curse and kill.

00:09:49.100 --> 00:09:51.070
How would they dare interfere?

00:09:51.070 --> 00:09:52.650
Isn't that so, boss?

00:09:54.400 --> 00:09:57.700
I'm not going to wipe up
your mess, Susutake.

00:09:57.700 --> 00:09:59.780
I know that!

00:09:59.780 --> 00:10:02.700
And you came to see me
because you want some information, right?

00:10:03.040 --> 00:10:06.500
I didn't know that there was information even you couldn't get, boss.

00:10:06.500 --> 00:10:09.080
Are you going to answer me or not?

00:10:09.080 --> 00:10:12.290
I will, but I want you
to listen to my story too!

00:10:12.290 --> 00:10:15.300
I was in jail until recently,
and I've been dying for a good conversation!

00:10:15.300 --> 00:10:17.220
It was probably because of your tattoo.

00:10:17.220 --> 00:10:18.720
Isn't it cool?

00:10:18.720 --> 00:10:22.850
These tattoos are used to mark people
who've been banished from Osaka to Edo.

00:10:22.850 --> 00:10:25.770
And because you have that, you got arrested.

00:10:25.770 --> 00:10:26.350
You idiot.

00:10:26.770 --> 00:10:30.440
Just tell me whether you've seen Tsuyukusa.

00:10:30.440 --> 00:10:31.730
Tsuyukusa?

00:10:31.730 --> 00:10:34.110
Oh, that impudent brat.

00:10:34.110 --> 00:10:35.480
I haven't seen him.

00:10:35.480 --> 00:10:37.360
Have there been any incidents?

00:10:38.240 --> 00:10:43.450
I heard there was a murder in a backstreet,
and a jailbreak as well.

00:10:43.450 --> 00:10:45.370
Those aren't related.

00:10:45.370 --> 00:10:48.580
Can you truly say that
demons weren't involved?

00:10:49.120 --> 00:10:53.460
Yeah, because this is the person
who broke out of jail.

00:10:57.260 --> 00:10:59.800
You might not think he's
a good doctor, but he is.

00:11:00.590 --> 00:11:03.100
Why is an escapee here?

00:11:03.100 --> 00:11:04.350
I helped him,

00:11:04.720 --> 00:11:07.980
because we became friends
when we were locked in the same cell.

00:11:07.980 --> 00:11:11.150
After hearing his story, I think he's innocent.

00:11:11.150 --> 00:11:16.440
I had a lot of medicine that I'd made myself to use in surgery.

00:11:16.440 --> 00:11:19.190
The drugs were all stolen.

00:11:19.190 --> 00:11:20.820
Was that opium?

00:11:20.820 --> 00:11:22.870
It's a painkiller.

00:11:22.870 --> 00:11:26.330
This robber seemingly tried to sell the drugs.

00:11:27.330 --> 00:11:31.210
An officer mistook me for the mastermind
behind the scenes and arrested me.

00:11:31.210 --> 00:11:33.250
When I was in trouble, this man helped.

00:11:33.250 --> 00:11:36.000
How's that? I'm pretty cool, right?!

00:11:36.000 --> 00:11:36.920
Shut up.

00:11:38.050 --> 00:11:39.970
Breaking out of jail went well,

00:11:40.590 --> 00:11:43.680
but for a while, it will be dangerous
to be out and about,

00:11:43.680 --> 00:11:46.350
so I asked if I could hide here.

00:11:47.680 --> 00:11:52.350
And while we were here,
the robber was killed.

00:11:52.690 --> 00:11:56.610
He probably ran into trouble with some low-life while dealing the drugs.

00:11:58.110 --> 00:12:01.200
Yeah, it doesn't seem related to Tsuyukusa.

00:12:03.320 --> 00:12:05.660
Oh, hey, a-are you going out?

00:12:05.660 --> 00:12:07.580
Hey, you guys! I'll be out for a bit.

00:12:07.580 --> 00:12:09.330
I'll take care of your sake.

00:12:15.250 --> 00:12:15.920
Utsubushi!

00:12:21.260 --> 00:12:23.510
Wow! That's a huge bird!

00:12:23.510 --> 00:12:24.760
Is it also a demon?

00:12:27.810 --> 00:12:31.020
So, Utsubushi, is there any
sign of Tsuyukusa yet?

00:12:31.480 --> 00:12:33.390
I still can't find him.

00:12:33.390 --> 00:12:36.900
But I found something that drew my attention, so I brought it.

00:12:37.400 --> 00:12:39.110
Drew your attention?

00:12:52.160 --> 00:12:53.620
He isn't from around here.

00:12:53.620 --> 00:12:54.580
He doesn't do illegal things.

00:12:55.120 --> 00:12:58.090
He smells slightly of Tsuyukusa.

00:12:58.090 --> 00:13:02.590
The herbs used to treat his wounds seem to be Tsuyukusa's.

00:13:08.510 --> 00:13:09.600
He woke up.

00:13:15.020 --> 00:13:17.520
You know Tsuyukusa, right?

00:13:18.190 --> 00:13:19.480
Where is he?

00:13:20.860 --> 00:13:22.990
D-Do you know him?!

00:13:23.400 --> 00:13:24.990
Please help me!

00:13:26.070 --> 00:13:30.950
Take me to Tsuyukusa.
I have to see him again.

00:13:35.330 --> 00:13:39.460
I've been investigating for a while,
but there's nothing strange.

00:13:40.500 --> 00:13:43.460
There don't seem to be any other monsters.

00:13:43.960 --> 00:13:47.090
He might have called another
monk for purification.

00:13:49.470 --> 00:13:50.720
What's this?

00:13:53.310 --> 00:13:54.850
Dust from this warehouse?

00:13:55.430 --> 00:13:56.560
No.

00:13:57.310 --> 00:13:58.440
This is...

00:14:02.440 --> 00:14:04.610
Please take care of our guests.

00:14:04.610 --> 00:14:05.990
Gotcha. Have a nice trip.

00:14:05.990 --> 00:14:07.200
Be careful.

00:14:07.200 --> 00:14:09.910
Will the two of them be
all right by themselves?

00:14:09.910 --> 00:14:12.950
Now, now, how about
some tea inside, guest?

00:14:12.950 --> 00:14:14.830
Ah, yes, thank you.

00:14:14.830 --> 00:14:17.660
Well, what kind of actor are you?

00:14:19.500 --> 00:14:21.540
I knew it!

00:14:21.540 --> 00:14:23.130
You're the boy I met back then.

00:14:23.130 --> 00:14:24.760
You attract attention,
so I recognized you easily.

00:14:25.170 --> 00:14:27.630
Oh, the old lady doctor from back then!

00:14:28.220 --> 00:14:29.680
Well, I'm glad.

00:14:29.680 --> 00:14:31.720
You didn't forget me.

00:14:31.720 --> 00:14:35.180
I'm sorry that I couldn't
help you that time.

00:14:35.180 --> 00:14:37.060
No, no, you don't have to apologize.

00:14:37.060 --> 00:14:39.100
Just being examined was a relief.

00:14:39.850 --> 00:14:43.440
By the way, why are you in this pharmacy?

00:14:43.440 --> 00:14:45.940
Oh, no, did it get worse?

00:14:45.940 --> 00:14:47.990
Ah, no, my eye is fine.

00:14:47.990 --> 00:14:49.490
I'm here on business for a friend.

00:14:49.490 --> 00:14:50.530
Friend?

00:14:50.530 --> 00:14:54.160
Oh, so I guess you came here with Shamon.

00:14:54.160 --> 00:14:55.370
Huh? Shamon-san?

00:14:55.660 --> 00:14:57.120
Oh, am I wrong?

00:14:57.120 --> 00:14:58.460
Isn't that right, Sakichi-san?

00:14:58.460 --> 00:15:02.580
Yes. I heard that he's at Nakamura-ya, which is quite nearby.

00:15:04.630 --> 00:15:07.010
I'm sensing someone who is frankly happy.

00:15:07.010 --> 00:15:08.840
I mustn't turn around.
I mustn't turn around!

00:15:09.130 --> 00:15:11.550
O-Oh, you were here too.

00:15:11.550 --> 00:15:14.600
It's unusual for you to come out here.

00:15:15.010 --> 00:15:17.640
It proved to be unavoidable.

00:15:17.640 --> 00:15:20.270
Is Shamon-sama here on business?

00:15:20.270 --> 00:15:21.690
Or is it just a private visit?

00:15:22.060 --> 00:15:26.780
I don't know, but he seemed quite troubled.

00:15:27.360 --> 00:15:30.530
But then again, I didn't hear about any unfortunate events at Nakamura-ya.

00:15:31.530 --> 00:15:34.030
Well, I'll be leaving now.

00:15:38.620 --> 00:15:40.250
H-Hey, Kuchiha.

00:15:41.960 --> 00:15:43.130
What a coincidence.

00:15:43.130 --> 00:15:45.380
Shamon-sama also came to this neighborhood.

00:15:47.000 --> 00:15:48.510
She's not bothered.

00:15:48.510 --> 00:15:49.970
How can she stand it?

00:15:49.970 --> 00:15:53.470
Hey, where do you think Nakamura-ya is?

00:15:54.600 --> 00:15:56.180
You're not listening.

00:15:57.760 --> 00:15:58.600
Hey.

00:15:59.100 --> 00:16:01.310
Oh? You want to know
where Nakamura-ya-san is?

00:16:01.690 --> 00:16:03.350
It's quite close.

00:16:03.350 --> 00:16:06.440
If you want, I don't mind
bringing you a map.

00:16:07.150 --> 00:16:10.190
This map is for doctors
to use on their rounds.

00:16:10.190 --> 00:16:10.940
Wow.

00:16:11.280 --> 00:16:13.280
Our Yorozu-ya is right here.

00:16:13.280 --> 00:16:15.660
And Nakamura-ya-san is here.

00:16:15.660 --> 00:16:18.450
This map has a somewhat larger scale.

00:16:19.910 --> 00:16:21.460
This is Nihonbashi.

00:16:21.460 --> 00:16:24.790
And this area is Naitou-Shinjuku,
where my brother and the young lady went.

00:16:24.790 --> 00:16:26.790
This is Ookawa.

00:16:26.790 --> 00:16:30.380
I see. This world was Japan's past.

00:16:30.380 --> 00:16:32.630
It's not surprising that some
places are familiar to me.

00:16:33.510 --> 00:16:37.180
If this is Sumidagawa, then around this
Shinobazunoike must be Ueno in my world.

00:16:41.430 --> 00:16:42.520
Toki?

00:16:43.190 --> 00:16:45.600
Um, it's nothing.

00:16:46.690 --> 00:16:50.820
I felt a connection with my world,
and it made me feel a bit lonely.

00:16:52.320 --> 00:16:54.320
But isn't it strange?

00:16:54.320 --> 00:16:56.950
That Shamon-sama came
all the way out here.

00:16:57.910 --> 00:17:00.580
Usually, clients come to his temple
to ask for help.

00:17:00.580 --> 00:17:01.950
And if it's not a Buddhist funeral service,

00:17:02.370 --> 00:17:05.330
then the last possibility is demons.

00:17:06.830 --> 00:17:09.880
We really have to check this out.

00:17:09.880 --> 00:17:11.340
Where are you going?

00:17:12.050 --> 00:17:13.420
Can I go with you?

00:17:14.380 --> 00:17:19.930
Oh, um, well, it'd be dangerous
to take you with us.

00:17:20.850 --> 00:17:23.060
There might be demons.

00:17:23.060 --> 00:17:24.810
No, I'll go with you!

00:17:25.730 --> 00:17:26.810
Shinshu-chan.

00:17:28.190 --> 00:17:31.440
I want to... I also want to do something!

00:17:31.440 --> 00:17:33.110
Don't leave me!

00:17:33.110 --> 00:17:34.530
I don't want to be alone.

00:17:35.360 --> 00:17:37.700
Then I'll go alone.

00:17:38.570 --> 00:17:39.700
You mustn't go alone, Kuchiha!

00:17:39.700 --> 00:17:41.990
Why can't we go all together?

00:17:41.990 --> 00:17:43.200
Shut up!

00:17:43.200 --> 00:17:45.080
How can we take you with us?!

00:17:45.830 --> 00:17:48.130
Why? Why?

00:17:48.130 --> 00:17:50.710
Didn't he say that there might be demons?!

00:17:50.710 --> 00:17:51.960
I'm not scared!

00:17:51.960 --> 00:17:53.710
That's not the issue!

00:17:53.710 --> 00:17:55.720
I'm telling you that you'll be in the way.

00:17:55.720 --> 00:17:57.430
You're such a disobedient girl.

00:17:57.430 --> 00:18:00.180
I won't be in the way!

00:18:00.180 --> 00:18:03.140
Hey, hey, handsome.
Aren't you going to stop them?

00:18:03.140 --> 00:18:05.350
It's tough being handsome, huh?

00:18:05.350 --> 00:18:08.900
Hey, Sakichi. How dare you
talk like that to a guest?

00:18:08.900 --> 00:18:10.400
Gotcha. Sorry, ma'am.

00:18:10.940 --> 00:18:15.530
Toki-san and Kuchiha-san seem to have
important business, so they're going out.

00:18:15.530 --> 00:18:17.070
Prepare to send the two
of them on their way.

00:18:17.070 --> 00:18:18.320
Gotcha.

00:18:18.320 --> 00:18:20.950
No, not just two, I'm going too.

00:18:22.620 --> 00:18:25.450
Please understand, Princess.

00:18:25.450 --> 00:18:27.620
In fact, you do understand, don't you?

00:18:28.790 --> 00:18:32.500
It would be better if Toki-san and Kuchiha-san went by themselves,

00:18:32.500 --> 00:18:35.340
and you remained here.

00:18:37.970 --> 00:18:39.130
Right?

00:18:39.630 --> 00:18:42.640
You two should also come
back as soon as possible.

00:18:43.260 --> 00:18:47.180
My brother might be quite angry
if you two weren't here.

00:18:48.020 --> 00:18:52.190
Um, yes, well, but is this really all right?

00:18:52.560 --> 00:18:54.270
Please count on me.

00:18:57.110 --> 00:18:58.900
Sorry, Shinshu-chan.

00:18:58.900 --> 00:19:01.910
I'll be back soon.
So will you wait for a while?

00:19:03.990 --> 00:19:05.660
Never mind. It's all right.

00:19:06.620 --> 00:19:08.910
Because you're nice to her,

00:19:08.910 --> 00:19:11.750
she seems to equate you
with Ginshu-sama without noticing.

00:19:12.790 --> 00:19:13.750
Beni-san.

00:19:16.340 --> 00:19:18.340
Now, if it's been decided, get going.

00:19:18.340 --> 00:19:19.260
Hey, Beni-san!

00:19:20.510 --> 00:19:21.760
Gotcha.

00:19:24.260 --> 00:19:26.260
Have a safe trip.

00:19:28.100 --> 00:19:30.890
Still, Toki, was this really a good idea?

00:19:30.890 --> 00:19:32.730
Shouldn't we stay close to her?

00:19:35.900 --> 00:19:40.240
Yeah, but she's probably safer
if I'm not with her.

00:19:40.780 --> 00:19:46.540
She... Beni-san might be in the same line of work as Kurotobi-san.

00:19:46.540 --> 00:19:48.250
Her hands were like yours.

00:19:48.250 --> 00:19:49.120
My hands?

00:19:49.660 --> 00:19:50.750
Yeah.

00:19:50.750 --> 00:19:57.300
Even rich young women who work hard
don't have such strong hands.

00:19:57.300 --> 00:19:59.840
Kuchiha, your hands are
those of a swordsman.

00:20:01.800 --> 00:20:03.260
I see.

00:20:03.260 --> 00:20:05.050
I do understand...

00:20:05.720 --> 00:20:07.100
But it's kinda callused.

00:20:07.100 --> 00:20:08.770
Huh? Why? Huh?

00:20:08.770 --> 00:20:10.890
Hm, I don't know.

00:20:11.940 --> 00:20:15.650
I was taking Tsuyukusa to Nakamura-ya.

00:20:16.270 --> 00:20:19.360
And we met a monster on the way.

00:20:20.110 --> 00:20:21.110
Um...

00:20:21.490 --> 00:20:24.200
You're making me feel
uncomfortable about talking.

00:20:24.200 --> 00:20:25.660
What?

00:20:25.660 --> 00:20:26.990
Stop it, Susutake.

00:20:27.660 --> 00:20:30.950
I somehow understand how you and Tsuyukusa are related.

00:20:30.950 --> 00:20:34.580
He seems to be accompanying that fox.

00:20:34.580 --> 00:20:39.500
Then to solve this, we just have to find the fox and beat it.

00:20:39.500 --> 00:20:42.880
Utsubushi, can you trace
the fox by its smell?

00:20:42.880 --> 00:20:43.970
Impossible.

00:20:43.970 --> 00:20:46.390
I've never met it, so I don't know its smell.

00:20:46.850 --> 00:20:49.430
Then can't you trace it by
the smell of human blood?

00:20:49.430 --> 00:20:53.230
That man over there stinks
even more of blood.

00:20:53.230 --> 00:20:54.480
You say I stink?

00:20:55.060 --> 00:21:01.070
Hey, Bon. Even if we find Tsuyukusa, what if he was helping the fox?

00:21:01.530 --> 00:21:04.070
Are you going to help him,
or are you going to take him back?

00:21:04.780 --> 00:21:08.990
You decide everything by yourself and never tell me anything.

00:21:08.990 --> 00:21:10.990
Don't you think that's unfriendly?

00:21:14.830 --> 00:21:18.380
H-Hey, are you going to see him?

00:21:18.380 --> 00:21:21.050
It might not be helpful,
but I'll tell you everything,

00:21:21.050 --> 00:21:22.960
so take me along too!

00:21:24.010 --> 00:21:25.680
You don't have to speak.

00:21:29.180 --> 00:21:29.930
What?

00:21:36.770 --> 00:21:39.230
It's gross, as usual.

00:21:39.230 --> 00:21:42.940
Brilliant, as usual, if something must be said.

00:21:42.940 --> 00:21:45.110
It's quicker this way.
